<worksheet xml:id="sec-quiz-describing-categorical-data-att-1">
  <title>Quiz: Describing Categorical Data Attempt 1</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      Name: <fillin characters="45"/>
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <exercise xml:id="ex-quiz-cat-data-att-1-population-sample-variable" workspace="0.3in">
    <statement>
      <p>
        A researcher wants to describe the choices made by students at a
        college when they play rock-paper-scissors. The researcher randomly
        selects 100 students from the college and records each student's
        choice in one round of the game.
      </p>
      <ol marker="a)">
        <li><p>Identify the population.</p></li>
        <li><p>Identify the sample.</p></li>
        <li>
          <p>
            Identify the variable being recorded. Is it categorical or numerical?
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

  <exercise xml:id="ex-quiz-cat-data-att-1-bike-rentals" workspace="0.1in">
    <statement>
      <p>
        A bike shop rents road, mountain, hybrid, and cruiser bikes.
        The manager takes a random sample of rentals and records the type
        of bike rented. The results are shown in the bar graph.
      </p>

      <image source="images/quiz-cat-data-att-1-bikes.png" width="80%">
        <description>
          Bar graph titled Bike Rentals in the Sample. The horizontal axis
          lists the bike types, and the vertical axis shows the number of
          rentals from 0 to 16, with labeled ticks every 2 rentals and
          gridlines every 1 rental. The bar heights are
          Road, 8; Mountain, 12; Hybrid, 15; and Cruiser, 5.
        </description>
      </image>

      <ol marker="a)">
        <li>
          <p>
            Complete the frequency and relative frequency table, including
            the total row. Give relative frequencies as decimals rounded
            to three decimal places.
          </p>
          <tabular row-headers="yes" halign="center" valign="middle"
                   top="medium" left="medium" bottom="medium" right="medium">
            <row header="yes" bottom="medium">
              <cell>Type of Bike</cell>
              <cell>Frequency</cell>
              <cell>Relative Frequency</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Road</cell>
              <cell></cell>
              <cell></cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Mountain</cell>
              <cell></cell>
              <cell></cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Hybrid</cell>
              <cell></cell>
              <cell></cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Cruiser</cell>
              <cell></cell>
              <cell></cell>
            </row>
            <row top="medium">
              <cell>Total</cell>
              <cell></cell>
              <cell></cell>
            </row>
          </tabular>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            What percentage of the rentals in the sample were not cruiser
            bikes? Round to one decimal place.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

  <exercise xml:id="ex-quiz-cat-data-att-1-rattlesnake-sightings" workspace="0.4in">
    <statement>
      <p>
        A park service records reported rattlesnake sightings on two trails.
        The stacked bar graph shows the counts for three years. The lower,
        solid segment of each bar represents Bald Mountain Trail. The upper,
        striped segment represents Camel Back Trail.
      </p>

      <image source="images/quiz-cat-data-att-1-rattlesnakes.png" width="80%">
        <description>
          Stacked bar graph titled Reported Rattlesnake Sightings. The
          horizontal axis lists 2023, 2024, and 2025. The vertical axis shows
          the number of sightings from 0 to 18 in increments of 2. In 2023,
          the lower, solid segment extends from 0 to 8 and the upper,
          striped segment extends from 8 to 14. In 2024, the lower segment
          extends from 0 to 12 and the upper segment extends from 12 to 16.
          In 2025, the lower segment extends from 0 to 6 and the upper
          segment extends from 6 to 16.
        </description>
      </image>

      <ol marker="a)">
        <li>
          <p>
            Use the graph to complete the contingency table, including all
            row and column totals.
          </p>
          <tabular row-headers="yes" halign="center" valign="middle"
                   top="medium" left="medium" bottom="medium" right="medium">
            <row header="yes" bottom="medium">
              <cell>Trail</cell>
              <cell>2023</cell>
              <cell>2024</cell>
              <cell>2025</cell>
              <cell>Total</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Bald Mountain</cell>
              <cell></cell>
              <cell></cell>
              <cell></cell>
              <cell></cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>Camel Back</cell>
              <cell></cell>
              <cell></cell>
              <cell></cell>
              <cell></cell>
            </row>
            <row top="medium">
              <cell>Total</cell>
              <cell></cell>
              <cell></cell>
              <cell></cell>
              <cell></cell>
            </row>
          </tabular>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            What percentage of the sightings reported in 2025 were on Bald
            Mountain Trail? Round to one decimal place.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </statement>
  </exercise>
</worksheet>
